{"schema":"baxy.message-compose-diagnostic.v2","trace":"t9","stage":"first","intent":"conversation","language":"mixed","greeting":"none","payload_keys":["kind"],"reason":"","finish_reason":"stop","followup_subject":"","published":true,"draft_bytes":466,"draft_sha256":"1ef495b7592f7546d8434c82ab27f2f2126765bc645d01f88ba57f82dc081b2a","payload":{"kind":"conversation"},"situation":"{\"kind\":\"conversation\",\"polarity\":\"success\"}","draft":"Una copia de seguridad es un archivo o conjunto de archivos que se almacenan aparte para proteger los datos originales. In case of loss, corruption, or accident, you can restore the original data from this backup. It's a way to ensure that your information isn't lost permanently. A backup can be stored on an external drive, cloud service, or another device. If something goes wrong with the main system, you can always go back to a previous state using the backup."}
